1
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:02,979
I've been listening to you this whole
time, and you're being incredibly rude.

2
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:06,720
Didn't you used to look at me
like I was a total nuisance?

3
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:07,899
Talk about rude.

4
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:08,980
Because you were annoying.

5
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:10,700
Always trying to pick a fight.

6
00:00:10,710 --> 00:00:12,696
- Fine, let's settle this once and for all.
- You're so annoying.

7
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:14,780
Let's see who's more
worthy of being his rival.

8
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:16,559
As far as he's concerned,
his ultimate rival...

9
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:17,760
It's you, isn't it?

10
00:00:17,930 --> 00:00:19,600
Maybe for now.

11
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:21,969
But what if I get the
top sales in Division 2?

12
00:00:21,970 --> 00:00:24,490
He'll have no choice but
to notice me then, right?

13
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:27,120
You think I'm just going
to hand you the top spot?

14
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:30,260
Don't underestimate me.

15
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:32,200
Fine.

16
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:33,450
Since you're going that far...

17
00:00:33,451 --> 00:00:34,931
This little competition between us...

18
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:36,540
is on.

19
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:39,000
"Fake Fact Lips"

20
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:43,199
(Episode 8: How should
I put it, it's already...)

21
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,280
- Good work today.
- Good work.

22
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:54,230
Oh.

23
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:55,630
Working overtime?

24
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:57,800
Keep up the good work.

25
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:02,060
You're so slow.

26
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:05,820
And they call you a star
employee. What a joke.

27
00:02:06,210 --> 00:02:07,249
Unlike you,

28
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:09,530
I'm not just wasting time here.

29
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,560
I just have work
that I want to finish today.

30
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,620
Because I can't afford to lose to you.

31
00:02:15,710 --> 00:02:17,819
Why don't you focus on
working instead of talking?

32
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:19,320
I am working.

33
00:02:20,010 --> 00:02:21,759
My hands are practically
getting tendonitis.

34
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:22,760
Shut up.

35
00:02:22,761 --> 00:02:24,161
Did you come here just to annoy me?

36
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:25,500
I'm scoping out the competition.

37
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:29,039
I don't need cheap
tricks against my rivals.

38
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:30,359
I may have accepted your challenge,

39
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,019
but I don't even consider you a rival.

40
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,020
You've got a big mouth.

41
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:36,180
Enjoy acting smug while you still can.

42
00:02:36,650 --> 00:02:39,399
Things have been pretty
tense between them lately.

43
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,910
Shito-san and Futami-san.

44
00:02:41,660 --> 00:02:42,990
Did they get into a fight?

45
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:44,080
You didn't know?

46
00:02:44,410 --> 00:02:46,096
Those two are in a fierce
competition right now.

47
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:46,870
Huh? Why?

48
00:02:46,910 --> 00:02:48,556
What about the competition
with Yotsuya-san?

49
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:49,580
Who knows?

50
00:02:50,250 --> 00:02:52,380
Futami-san is really capable, after all.

51
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:55,460
Oh.

52
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:59,820
I heard Futami-san landed
the Alfd System contract.

53
00:02:59,860 --> 00:03:02,499
Apparently, he won over
that difficult client in no time.

54
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:05,060
Man, that Kansai charm is something else.

55
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:07,940
- Good work.
- Oh, Yotsuya-san.

56
00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:09,279
Where's Shito?

57
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:11,280
Locked in a fierce battle over there.

58
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:12,940
You're being so loud.

59
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:13,660
You're the loud one.

60
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:14,120
I can't even concentrate.

61
00:03:14,121 --> 00:03:15,459
You're definitely the louder one here.

62
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:17,060
- Shut up.
- What is your problem?

63
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:19,020
Has Yotsuya-san already
dropped out of the race?

64
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:31,079
That Moncler contract
even you couldn't land...

65
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:33,090
is keeping me incredibly busy right now.

66
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:35,889
It's just the first contract
you've landed since coming here.

67
00:03:35,890 --> 00:03:37,780
Don't let it go to your head.

68
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:38,840
Hmph.

69
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:41,859
This is a glorious first step
toward becoming number one in Division 2.

70
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:44,499
Hey, you two need to cut it out.

71
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:45,550
Shut up.

72
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:48,660
This has nothing to do with you.

73
00:03:49,433 --> 00:03:50,993
Sorry, Yotsuya.

74
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:53,850
This is between him and me.

75
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,390
Right...

76
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:23,380
Ryo.

77
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:31,220
Zen...

78
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:42,480
Sorry about earlier.

79
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:45,090
Is something on your mind?

80
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,550
No, it's just...

81
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:50,740
about that trip we talked about.

82
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:51,980
The one for your birthday.

83
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:53,820
Oh.

84
00:04:54,210 --> 00:04:55,210
Like the accommodations.

85
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:58,420
I thought we should
probably finalize it soon.

86
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:03,740
If you don't mind,

87
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:07,070
would you like me to arrange it?

88
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:09,279
No, I'd feel bad leaving it all to you...

89
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:10,280
It's fine.

90
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:13,340
I actually love planning things like this.

91
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,080
Thanks. In that case, could you handle it?

92
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:19,320
Of course.

93
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:22,400
You must be busy too.

94
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:24,780
Aren't you?

95
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:29,480
But I can't lose to Futami.

96
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:33,300
He might act like that,
but he's actually really good at his job.

97
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:37,180
So you two really are competing.

98
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:39,240
That showdown...

99
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:42,560
No, he's just the one picking a fight.

100
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:49,500
Then why don't you just ignore him?

101
00:05:51,310 --> 00:05:52,340
Huh?

102
00:05:53,660 --> 00:05:55,700
Why are you taking
this so seriously anyway?

103
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:02,560
"I'm a better match for Yotsuya than you."

104
00:06:04,180 --> 00:06:05,280
No...

105
00:06:07,610 --> 00:06:08,840
Shito.

106
00:06:11,370 --> 00:06:14,370
The superior one is heading home first.

107
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:19,260
I'll get back to work then.

108
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:20,420
Wait...

109
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:33,000
Futami.

110
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:40,560
- Hey...
- Yeah?

111
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:43,220
This competition between you and Shito...

112
00:06:43,760 --> 00:06:47,560
Can't you compete with me instead?

113
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:48,940
Huh?

114
00:06:49,030 --> 00:06:50,050
I mean...

115
00:06:50,450 --> 00:06:52,219
Forget Shito. Just compete with me...

116
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:53,220
No way.

117
00:06:54,410 --> 00:06:55,410
Why not?

118
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:57,500
I have to beat Shito first.

119
00:06:57,540 --> 00:06:59,316
Otherwise, it wouldn't be
any fun for you, Yotsuya.

120
00:06:59,340 --> 00:07:00,340
No...

121
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:01,210
That's not true...

122
00:07:01,211 --> 00:07:03,990
Besides, I have something on the line.

123
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:06,230
What's that?

124
00:07:06,590 --> 00:07:07,650
It's a secret.

125
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:09,500
Oh.

126
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:12,300
By the way, I'm going on
a business trip tomorrow.

127
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:14,039
With Shito.

128
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,070
What?

129
00:07:15,930 --> 00:07:17,390
I didn't hear about this.

130
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:19,480
Of course not.

131
00:07:20,140 --> 00:07:21,980
We're not even in the same department.

132
00:07:22,770 --> 00:07:23,770
Well,

133
00:07:24,860 --> 00:07:28,880
I'll make sure to get some great results.

134
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:39,060
I don't know...

135
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:44,800
Honestly...

136
00:08:05,980 --> 00:08:08,300
Handing this project over
to you makes me so nervous.

137
00:08:09,206 --> 00:08:10,386
Don't worry.

138
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:13,080
I'll show you I can do a
much better job than you.

139
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,539
You're certainly confident.

140
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:16,640
You two are the same.

141
00:08:17,900 --> 00:08:18,900
"You two"?

142
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:21,000
About Yotsuya, of course.

143
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,310
You bring him up every chance you get.

144
00:08:27,630 --> 00:08:30,510
Why are you so obsessed
with Yotsuya anyway?

145
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:32,300
Oh?

146
00:08:33,140 --> 00:08:34,260
Are you actually interested?

147
00:08:34,560 --> 00:08:35,420
Not really...

148
00:08:35,430 --> 00:08:36,859
You sure you don't want to hear it?

149
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:37,860
I'm good.

150
00:08:38,800 --> 00:08:40,536
This is the part where
you're supposed to ask.

151
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:42,560
I told you, I'm not interested.

152
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:44,440
Yotsuya...

153
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:46,820
You're really going to tell me, aren't you?

154
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:50,850
He is very special to me.

155
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:57,500
My family didn't get along very well.

156
00:08:59,300 --> 00:09:00,949
I chose my own path for the future,

157
00:09:00,950 --> 00:09:02,470
despite my parents' opposition.

158
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:04,560
And then,

159
00:09:04,583 --> 00:09:07,143
after I met him in college,

160
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:12,800
I'd sometimes wonder
if I had made the right choice.

161
00:09:14,470 --> 00:09:15,550
I get that.

162
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:17,780
Me too.

163
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:20,619
My relationship with my
dad used to be pretty strained.

164
00:09:20,620 --> 00:09:22,220
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

165
00:09:22,310 --> 00:09:23,760
He was a very strict man.

166
00:09:24,430 --> 00:09:25,440
Oh.

167
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:27,180
That's surprising.

168
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:30,390
I didn't think you'd have
those kinds of issues.

169
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:33,440
Well, a lot happened,

170
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:35,800
but we're fine now.

171
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,120
Oh.

172
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:39,000
Did you make up?

173
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:41,520
Because I realized

174
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:44,200
that this is my life.

175
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:46,780
Yeah.

176
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:50,240
From then on, no matter what my dad said,

177
00:09:50,980 --> 00:09:53,290
I started making my own decisions.

178
00:09:55,740 --> 00:09:57,970
Eventually, he just stopped
trying to lecture me.

179
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:05,810
I think as long as it's a path you chose,

180
00:10:06,190 --> 00:10:07,640
you should be confident in it.

181
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:14,260
Yeah...

182
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:17,240
Because,

183
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:20,710
even if you live up to your
parents' expectations, Futami,

184
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:23,950
they won't necessarily live up to yours.

185
00:10:27,290 --> 00:10:30,370
You're right.

186
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:35,880
Those words really struck
a chord with me back then.

187
00:10:36,980 --> 00:10:38,500
It felt like a huge weight was lifted.

188
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:44,050
That's why I respect Yotsuya.

189
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:50,840
What's with that look on your face?

190
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:53,500
Nothing.

191
00:10:54,096 --> 00:10:56,006
I hate to ruin your trip down memory lane,

192
00:10:56,540 --> 00:10:59,380
but those are the exact words
I said to Yotsuya in high school.

193
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:01,660
Don't talk nonsense.

194
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:03,159
There's no way.

195
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:04,080
If you think I'm lying,

196
00:11:04,081 --> 00:11:05,820
go ask Yotsuya yourself.

197
00:11:10,380 --> 00:11:11,580
Then doesn't that mean...

198
00:11:12,290 --> 00:11:15,750
I've been saved by your
words this whole time?

199
00:11:16,920 --> 00:11:17,920
Looks like it.

200
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:21,080
This is the worst.

201
00:11:22,180 --> 00:11:24,460
But this also proves

202
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,279
that you can't beat me.

203
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:28,280
No.

204
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:30,660
That has nothing to do with this.

205
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:31,690
So?

206
00:11:32,020 --> 00:11:35,060
Who did you say was
worthy of Yotsuya again?

207
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:36,500
I told you, that was...

208
00:11:36,501 --> 00:11:40,569
- That was...
- After all, a well-matched relationship

209
00:11:40,570 --> 00:11:43,370
can't exist without equality, right?

210
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:45,279
Based on what you just said,

211
00:11:45,280 --> 00:11:48,410
your feelings for Yotsuya
are just one-sided admiration.

212
00:11:48,450 --> 00:11:49,899
Is that really equal?

213
00:11:49,900 --> 00:11:51,740
No, it's not.

214
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:52,840
Which means,

215
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:53,570
the current you

216
00:11:53,571 --> 00:11:55,640
can't stand on equal footing with Yotsuya.

217
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:19,050
Now then,

218
00:12:19,110 --> 00:12:21,310
you probably don't feel like
competing with me anymore.

219
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:23,140
Just stay quietly behind me.

220
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,560
Actually, it's quite the opposite.

221
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:28,980
I'm getting more and
more interested in you.

222
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:30,120
Huh?

223
00:12:30,580 --> 00:12:33,520
I think I want to get to know you better.

224
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:36,060
Stop joking around. Let's go.

225
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:37,500
Hey.

226
00:12:38,220 --> 00:12:39,300
Let's grab a drink tonight.

227
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,499
I have dinner with a client.

228
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:42,740
Then we can go after that.

229
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:44,340
You're so annoying.

230
00:12:44,550 --> 00:12:45,550
Exactly.

231
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,260
That's my best quality.

232
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:48,440
How should I know?

233
00:12:48,470 --> 00:12:49,970
Then you can start learning now.

234
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:51,799
Why on earth would I want to know that?

235
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:53,140
I want to get to know you,

236
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:54,800
so you should get to know me too.

237
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:58,410
Then...

238
00:12:58,770 --> 00:12:59,780
How about...

239
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:01,100
Let's compete again.

240
00:13:01,570 --> 00:13:03,340
Huh? Compete in what?

241
00:13:04,030 --> 00:13:06,010
What do you mean? A competition, of course.

242
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:11,400
Whoever makes it to the top first wins.

243
00:13:12,910 --> 00:13:14,250
You're on.

244
00:13:21,090 --> 00:13:22,090
You know...

245
00:13:22,580 --> 00:13:25,230
I think I prefer someone who
is worthy of being my rival.

246
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:26,540
Huh?

247
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:28,990
So, I'm sorry.

248
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:32,530
It's just not fun being with you anymore.

249
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:36,650
Wait.

250
00:13:57,560 --> 00:14:00,500
I'm such an easy mark...

251
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:25,460
Hello?

252
00:14:25,650 --> 00:14:27,320
Ah, sorry.

253
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:28,710
Did I wake you up?

254
00:14:28,910 --> 00:14:30,200
Oh, no, it's fine.

255
00:14:30,780 --> 00:14:33,260
But your voice sounds a bit off.

256
00:14:33,450 --> 00:14:35,300
I had quite a bit to drink.

257
00:14:36,210 --> 00:14:37,870
I just got back to the hotel.

258
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:39,200
I see.

259
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:43,180
Thanks for working so late.

260
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:47,670
Did you go to an after-party after dinner?

261
00:14:47,940 --> 00:14:49,319
No, after the dinner,

262
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:50,990
Futami and I went out for another drink.

263
00:14:51,180 --> 00:14:52,180
Oh...

264
00:14:52,470 --> 00:14:53,470
That's strange.

265
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:57,430
Didn't he say he'd take a photo
of us drinking and send it to you?

266
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:02,460
No, I didn't get anything.

267
00:15:03,740 --> 00:15:05,480
He probably just passed out in his room.

268
00:15:06,420 --> 00:15:08,000
Oh, by the way...

269
00:15:08,570 --> 00:15:10,980
I heard you told Futami the same thing
you once told Ryo?

270
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:12,600
Huh?

271
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:17,040
You know, the one about "Even if
you meet your parents' expectations..."

272
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:19,120
Ah, wait.

273
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:22,380
Futami told you about that?

274
00:15:23,290 --> 00:15:25,040
Wait, that's so embarrassing...

275
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:26,819
He was even bragging about it,

276
00:15:26,820 --> 00:15:29,540
saying it was something Yotsuya
said that really resonated with him.

277
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:31,880
Seriously?

278
00:15:32,930 --> 00:15:35,740
Maybe you two are actually quite similar.

279
00:15:36,390 --> 00:15:39,280
Somehow, talking to Futami

280
00:15:39,690 --> 00:15:42,430
reminds me of the old days
when we were just rivals.

281
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:50,000
The info about that inn,

282
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:52,420
I sent it to you. Did you check it?

283
00:15:52,740 --> 00:15:54,220
Yeah, I saw it.

284
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,090
- Thanks.
- Sure.

285
00:15:57,740 --> 00:16:00,640
I'm looking for restaurants now.

286
00:16:01,790 --> 00:16:03,560
I'll make sure you have a great time.

287
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:05,940
You don't have to go to so much trouble.

288
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:07,560
You're busy too.

289
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:13,820
Besides, just being able to relax
with you is enough for me.

290
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,200
Yeah.

291
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:18,810
I'm looking forward to it.

292
00:16:19,360 --> 00:16:20,360
Yeah.

293
00:16:20,930 --> 00:16:22,290
Zen...

294
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:26,960
I want to see you soon.

295
00:16:28,140 --> 00:16:29,140
Alright, alright.

296
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,120
I have to get up early
tomorrow, so I'm going to bed.

297
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:33,480
You should get some sleep too.

298
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:35,200
Yeah.

299
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,200
Good night.

300
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:40,940
Good night.

301
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:05,950
Actually, I want to see you too...

302
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:10,730
Why can't I just be honest and say it?

303
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:19,400
Ah...

304
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:23,280
Even though I'm back
from the business trip,

305
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:26,560
being in Tokyo still
doesn't feel like home.

306
00:17:27,320 --> 00:17:29,560
Then I'll head straight home in a bit.

307
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:30,680
Oh, really?

308
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:32,780
Then let's grab some food together.

309
00:17:33,130 --> 00:17:34,859
No, I have somewhere to go.

310
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:35,899
Where are you going?

311
00:17:35,900 --> 00:17:36,959
It has nothing to do with you.

312
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:38,540
Come on, just tell me.

313
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:42,320
I'm currently running
"Project Dig Deep into Shito."

314
00:17:42,980 --> 00:17:43,990
You're so annoying.

315
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:46,220
I'm just going shopping.

316
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:47,620
What are you buying?

317
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:51,120
For someone who always takes care of me.

318
00:17:51,680 --> 00:17:53,360
I thought I'd get him a gift.

319
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:54,720
Oh?

320
00:17:55,460 --> 00:17:57,499
You actually have an
unexpectedly cute side.

321
00:17:57,500 --> 00:17:58,540
Huh?

322
00:17:58,950 --> 00:17:59,950
Alright.

323
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:02,900
I'll help you pick it out.

324
00:18:02,910 --> 00:18:04,000
No, thanks.

325
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:05,320
Don't follow me.

326
00:18:06,660 --> 00:18:09,380
I'm coming anyway.

327
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:11,920
Hmm?

328
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:19,299
(Yotsuya Ryo: Are you back in Tokyo?
Want to grab dinner later?)

329
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:22,300
(Shito Zen: Sorry, I'm still working.)

330
00:18:32,290 --> 00:18:33,329
Good work today.

331
00:18:33,330 --> 00:18:34,830
Yeah, good work.

332
00:18:36,510 --> 00:18:40,050
Man, today's negotiations were tough too.

333
00:18:41,250 --> 00:18:42,690
Go home and get some rest.

334
00:18:42,870 --> 00:18:43,950
I will.

335
00:18:44,790 --> 00:18:45,910
What about you, Yotsuya-san?

336
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:48,520
I'll head out after
wrapping a few things up.

337
00:18:49,430 --> 00:18:51,270
Don't push yourself too hard.

338
00:18:51,790 --> 00:18:53,409
You don't look very well.

339
00:18:53,410 --> 00:18:54,410
I'm fine.

340
00:18:55,990 --> 00:18:58,910
Once I get through this, I have
something to look forward to this weekend.

341
00:18:59,130 --> 00:19:00,470
Oh, nice.

342
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:01,760
Is it with your girlfriend?

343
00:19:02,050 --> 00:19:03,110
Who knows?

344
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:05,220
Alright, go on, go home.

345
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:08,060
Then I'll take my leave. See you.

346
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:41,900
It's fine...

347
00:19:53,590 --> 00:19:54,950
So after all that, it's for a guy?

348
00:19:55,450 --> 00:19:56,450
What about it?

349
00:19:57,610 --> 00:19:58,570
The way you were talking earlier,

350
00:19:58,571 --> 00:20:00,710
anyone would have thought
it was a gift for a lover.

351
00:20:01,470 --> 00:20:02,470
It's not like that.

352
00:20:03,450 --> 00:20:04,450
Sigh...

353
00:20:05,290 --> 00:20:06,430
How boring.

354
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:09,000
Then go home.

355
00:20:09,110 --> 00:20:10,110
No, wait.

356
00:20:11,330 --> 00:20:13,850
I actually wanted a tie too.

357
00:20:14,810 --> 00:20:15,869
By the way,

358
00:20:15,870 --> 00:20:17,940
who is this gift actually for?

359
00:20:19,050 --> 00:20:20,669
No one, just a friend...

360
00:20:20,670 --> 00:20:21,630
A regular friend.

361
00:20:21,631 --> 00:20:22,930
You have friends?

362
00:20:22,970 --> 00:20:24,180
That's so rude.

363
00:20:26,150 --> 00:20:29,020
Well, giving gifts is nice,

364
00:20:29,970 --> 00:20:31,970
but words are still the
most important thing.

365
00:20:33,530 --> 00:20:36,269
After all, expressing
your feelings directly

366
00:20:36,270 --> 00:20:37,710
is what touches people the most.

367
00:20:38,650 --> 00:20:39,819
Since you seem bad with words,

368
00:20:39,820 --> 00:20:41,060
that's my advice to you.

369
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:43,989
If I could say whatever I wanted like you,

370
00:20:43,990 --> 00:20:45,006
life would probably be a lot easier.

371
00:20:45,030 --> 00:20:46,030
Oh.

372
00:20:46,910 --> 00:20:47,780
Hmm?

373
00:20:47,910 --> 00:20:49,390
Hey, you're insulting me, aren't you?

374
00:21:20,650 --> 00:21:21,850
Still working...

375
00:21:23,950 --> 00:21:25,070
Doesn't look like it...

376
00:21:31,530 --> 00:21:32,970
Excuse me, I'd like to get out.

377
00:21:33,790 --> 00:21:37,040
I'll be right back. Could
you wait for me a moment?

378
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:38,270
I'll leave my bag here.

379
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:39,590
Excuse me.

380
00:21:39,630 --> 00:21:40,630
I'll be right back.

381
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:44,580
Zen.

382
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:47,380
Ryo.

383
00:21:47,850 --> 00:21:50,490
What are you doing here?

384
00:21:51,550 --> 00:21:53,760
- Are you heading home?
- Huh?

385
00:21:54,690 --> 00:21:55,950
Ah, yeah, sort of.

386
00:21:57,210 --> 00:22:00,620
Then come stay at my place tonight.

387
00:22:00,900 --> 00:22:02,210
Now?

388
00:22:02,650 --> 00:22:04,170
But...

389
00:22:06,430 --> 00:22:07,440
Is that okay?

390
00:22:08,990 --> 00:22:10,760
I even have the taxi waiting.

391
00:22:30,110 --> 00:22:31,110
I'm sorry.

392
00:22:31,990 --> 00:22:33,270
For dragging you over like this.

393
00:22:34,350 --> 00:22:35,350
Huh?

394
00:22:35,890 --> 00:22:38,560
Ah, no, that's fine.

395
00:22:48,850 --> 00:22:50,380
The business trip went well.

396
00:22:52,310 --> 00:22:54,260
And the handover to
Futami is pretty much done.

397
00:22:56,470 --> 00:22:57,470
I see.

398
00:22:58,810 --> 00:22:59,810
That's good.

399
00:23:05,090 --> 00:23:07,420
I think I'll take a nap
before we get there.

400
00:23:09,300 --> 00:23:10,300
Oh...

401
00:23:47,090 --> 00:23:48,090
Zen...

402
00:23:51,550 --> 00:23:53,240
Stay over tonight.

403
00:24:59,050 --> 00:25:01,450
(Final Episode Preview)
Don't you have anything to say to me?

404
00:25:02,070 --> 00:25:05,026
(Final Episode: It's a Full Moon Tonight)
More than not being able to see you,

405
00:25:05,050 --> 00:25:06,960
I hate it even more when
you won't lean on me.

406
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:08,380
I really am sorry.

407
00:25:08,510 --> 00:25:09,969
What happened between you two?

408
00:25:09,970 --> 00:25:11,940
Now you've ruined everything.

409
00:25:12,090 --> 00:25:13,529
We're not on equal footing right now.

410
00:25:13,530 --> 00:25:14,629
Huh?

411
00:25:14,630 --> 00:25:16,220
Just spit it out.

